1
00:00:20,239 --> 00:00:24,870
We did it.

2
00:00:27,280 --> 00:00:37,066
Everything is bigger in Texas, including the shock of this win.

3
00:00:39,679 --> 00:00:45,176
We shocked the world tonight.

4
00:00:45,176 --> 00:01:00,150
With a Texas chip on our shoulder, we showed that anything is possible.

5
00:01:00,160 --> 00:01:05,660
Because it never bothered me that they doubted me.

6
00:01:08,799 --> 00:01:11,180
It bothered me that they doubted us.

7
00:01:16,239 --> 00:01:24,550
Hundreds of millions on attack ads, written off over and over again.

8
00:01:25,890 --> 00:01:31,310
But Texas, my faith in you never wavered.

9
00:01:37,280 --> 00:01:39,560
I have spoken to Governor Abbott.

10
00:01:39,560 --> 00:01:46,380
He called to congratulate me.

11
00:01:50,297 --> 00:01:55,830
He extended a generous offer to assist with the transition.

12
00:01:59,810 --> 00:02:07,290
I want to thank him and his family for their years of service to this great state.

13
00:02:15,440 --> 00:02:37,530
And now I stand before you humbled and grateful and in awe of the incredible grace and power of God and of Texas.

14
00:02:43,520 --> 00:02:52,678
I am a daughter of the Rio Grande Valley.

15
00:03:11,040 --> 00:03:16,988
Where the people embody the work ethic and values of our great state.

16
00:03:18,080 --> 00:03:34,220
Where no one would have imagined that one day a little girl from the RGV would stand before you here as the next governor of the greatest state.

17
00:03:39,028 --> 00:03:46,750
But God had a plan.

18
00:03:46,750 --> 00:03:51,590
And the people of Texas had a plan, too.

19
00:03:54,380 --> 00:03:56,620
It was a plan I did not know.

20
00:03:57,760 --> 00:04:00,940
I never set out to be a politician.

21
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:03,420
I am a mom.

22
00:04:06,640 --> 00:04:13,608
I am a mom who loves her children, who believes in their teachers.

23
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:27,489
And who believes in Texas public schools.

24
00:04:43,874 --> 00:04:54,524
And when I saw my child's school under threat, I did what any mom would do.

25
00:04:54,524 --> 00:04:58,550
I fought back.

26
00:04:58,560 --> 00:05:07,130
I ran for the school board because I wanted my child and every Texas child to have the opportunity to succeed.

27
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:12,590
From the school board to the House of Representatives.

28
00:05:15,180 --> 00:05:32,334
And now with your extraordinary faith and the trust of the people of Texas to the governor's [inaudible].

29
00:05:42,880 --> 00:05:54,130
Only here, only here, where no matter where you come from, no matter how humble your beginnings, your life can be bigger than your dreams.

30
00:05:55,925 --> 00:06:05,320
When we started this campaign a little over a year ago, I asked a simple question.

31
00:06:06,440 --> 00:06:12,520
Is Texas a state that is by and for the people of Texas?

32
00:06:13,780 --> 00:06:20,260
Or is this the billionaire's world and we just live here?

33
00:06:24,479 --> 00:06:29,512
Does Texas belong to the parents and their children?

34
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:37,830
Or the billionaires trying to dismantle our schools.

35
00:06:37,830 --> 00:06:55,990
Does Texas belong to the farmers and ranchers who have worked this land for generations, or the corporations trying to buy it up?

36
00:06:56,000 --> 00:07:09,020
Does Texas belong to the working families who pay their taxes and do everything right, or the wealthy and well-connected who play by different rules?

37
00:07:12,110 --> 00:07:21,690
Does Texas belong to the people who rise before the sun, who work two jobs, who build our homes,

38
00:07:21,870 --> 00:07:29,970
Who keep our hospitals running, who put everything they've got into small businesses and big dreams?

39
00:07:32,866 --> 00:07:40,580
Or does it belong to the people who write the biggest check to politicians in Austin?

40
00:07:43,295 --> 00:07:54,706
Tonight, Texas, we answered and we did not whisper.

41
00:07:55,919 --> 00:08:12,156
We answered loud enough for every billionaire, every lobbyist, and every corrupt politician in Austin to hear: Texas belongs to us.

42
00:08:12,166 --> 00:08:26,310
It's a question we answered in McAllen and Corpus Christi, in Dallas and in Temple, in San Antonio and Lubbock.

43
00:08:26,320 --> 00:08:33,690
From the neighborhoods of Austin to the wide open skies of West Texas all the way out to Big Bend.

44
00:08:37,680 --> 00:08:51,240
We answered in our big cities where they tried to silence your voice with gerrymandered maps and closed polling sites only to see turnout like never before.

45
00:08:55,200 --> 00:09:00,880
And you answered in small towns where people have been told their vote was already spoken for.

46
00:09:01,860 --> 00:09:12,120
We answered in communities that politicians visit every four years to ask for your vote only to forget about you as soon as they get to Austin.

47
00:09:13,280 --> 00:09:21,780
We answered in places that have been overlooked, underestimated, and left behind for far too long.

48
00:09:22,700 --> 00:09:39,160
And we answered across party lines because this campaign was always about whether the people of Texas ought to have a government that belongs to them.

49
00:09:41,840 --> 00:09:47,410
Not the highest bidder, not the biggest donor, not the most powerful lobbyist.

50
00:09:47,410 --> 00:09:47,930
You.

51
00:09:51,440 --> 00:09:58,360
And I want to say something to the powerful people who have gotten very comfortable running this state.

52
00:10:03,518 --> 00:10:16,608
The voters have delivered a mandate for change, and it is change they will get.

53
00:10:24,240 --> 00:10:28,840
We will lead with a politics of courage, not convenience.

54
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:35,520
Progress will not be halted by partisanship, and Texas will bow down to no one.

55
00:10:36,923 --> 00:10:45,220
The days of treating our public schools like they are for sale are over.

56
00:10:48,713 --> 00:10:54,800
The days of treating our tax dollars like your personal piggy bank are over.

57
00:10:57,519 --> 00:11:04,322
The days of writing one set of rules for working people and another for the wealthy and well-connected are over.

58
00:11:07,340 --> 00:11:20,320
And the days of telling Texans to settle for less while only billionaires in boardrooms profit from a state we have all built — those days are over, Too.

59
00:11:21,180 --> 00:11:30,240
This state was built by people with calloused hands and tired feet.

60
00:11:30,240 --> 00:11:32,560
By teachers and nurses.

61
00:11:33,200 --> 00:11:36,940
By oilfield workers and truck drivers.

62
00:11:37,420 --> 00:11:42,880
By small-business owners who put everything they had on the line.

63
00:11:43,900 --> 00:11:49,200
By parents who sacrificed so their children could have a better life.

64
00:11:50,260 --> 00:11:56,940
And those are the people who should come first in the state they built.

65
00:11:58,144 --> 00:12:10,140
They have labored and maintained an American dream through a long hard night.

66
00:12:11,260 --> 00:12:13,940
My friends, it is morning now.

67
00:12:17,794 --> 00:12:20,965
Tomorrow, our transition begins.

68
00:12:20,965 --> 00:12:51,580
And in January, I will take the oath of office ready to lead a government by the people and for the people.

69
00:12:54,475 --> 00:13:06,910
Not for the people who donated the most, not for the people who know the right people, but for every single Texan.

70
00:13:06,920 --> 00:13:12,240
Because this governor's office does not belong to me.

71
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:15,460
It does not belong to my party.

72
00:13:16,660 --> 00:13:18,080
It belongs to you.

73
00:13:21,860 --> 00:13:23,576
This is our Texas.

74
00:13:23,576 --> 00:13:24,900
This is our government.

75
00:13:25,160 --> 00:13:28,120
And this is our one fight.

76
00:13:28,740 --> 00:13:30,920
And tonight we won.

77
00:13:42,480 --> 00:13:44,184
Let me be clear.

78
00:13:44,184 --> 00:13:50,530
We did not end one era of single party rule just to usher in another.

79
00:13:51,730 --> 00:14:03,370
The same national pundits and political class who ignored and then misunderstood this campaign will declare this a victory for Democrats.

80
00:14:04,290 --> 00:14:07,110
They continue to misunderstand.

81
00:14:07,810 --> 00:14:11,150
This victory is so much bigger.

82
00:14:11,950 --> 00:14:15,223
It belongs to Texas.

83
00:14:15,223 --> 00:14:25,740
It is a victory for taxpayers who work too hard to see their money handed out to donors and special interests.

84
00:14:26,260 --> 00:14:33,371
We will end the era of no bid contracts in Texas.

85
00:14:33,381 --> 00:14:40,040
And please listen, it is a victory for young people.

86
00:14:43,519 --> 00:14:53,490
Young people across our state who possess unimaginable talent but have been left feeling so little hope.

87
00:14:55,180 --> 00:15:03,432
You will never have to choose between the state you love and a job that'll pay your worth.

88
00:15:04,960 --> 00:15:10,430
You will have the economy that serves your ambitions, your dreams, and your hard work.

89
00:15:10,930 --> 00:15:16,070
A government on your side and the hope you deserve.

90
00:15:17,090 --> 00:15:28,391
This is a victory for teachers who will be paid what they are worth.

91
00:15:28,401 --> 00:16:00,986
And in case you have not heard, on day one, I will fire Mike Morath, and we will work tirelessly to repair the damage of the Texas voucher scam and end an

92
00:16:00,986 --> 00:16:04,583
Era in which our schools are sold for parts.

93
00:16:06,392 --> 00:16:12,150
This is a victory for the parents of Texas.

94
00:16:12,150 --> 00:16:22,550
We are taking our children's education back from a government that has failed them.

95
00:16:22,560 --> 00:16:25,532
Schools will not be taken out of our control.

96
00:16:25,532 --> 00:16:30,881
They will not be shuttered or suffocated.

97
00:16:31,480 --> 00:16:35,220
Being a parent is hard enough.

98
00:16:35,220 --> 00:16:39,680
Without carrying the burden of a government's failures.

99
00:16:42,240 --> 00:16:47,860
To the children of Texas, your schools will not close.

100
00:16:51,360 --> 00:17:04,411
You will be invested in and you will grow up in a Texas where you are lifted up every single day to reach your Godgiven potential.

101
00:17:05,342 --> 00:17:14,940
Tonight, I make a solemn promise to every single Texan.

102
00:17:16,060 --> 00:17:24,800
Whether you voted for me or Greg Abbott or felt so betrayed by a broken politics that you did not vote at all,

103
00:17:26,340 --> 00:17:37,620
Whether you're a Democrat, a Republican, or neither, no matter where you live, no matter what your expectations of me are,

104
00:17:38,540 --> 00:17:48,360
No matter how accustomed you've become to corruption and incompetence, to experiencing government as something that is done to you,

105
00:17:48,360 --> 00:17:52,810
Not with you, for you, or by you.

106
00:17:53,352 --> 00:17:59,190
Hear what Texas said today loud and clear.

107
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:04,880
Your government belongs to you.

108
00:18:09,533 --> 00:18:12,570
As your governor, I will never forget it.

109
00:18:13,010 --> 00:18:18,230
There will be no special set of rules for the wealthy and well-connected.

110
00:18:18,230 --> 00:18:22,770
No looking the other way when someone in my own party does wrong.

111
00:18:23,999 --> 00:18:29,890
No excuses for corruption because it comes from someone who shares my politics.

112
00:18:31,790 --> 00:18:35,210
Corruption does not become right when our side does it.

113
00:18:36,389 --> 00:18:41,470
Accountability does not stop at the doors of the governor's office.

114
00:18:41,810 --> 00:18:42,650
It begins there.

115
00:18:48,280 --> 00:18:52,200
The trust you have placed in me tonight is not a blank check.

116
00:18:52,960 --> 00:18:59,900
It is a sacred responsibility and I intend to earn it every single day.

117
00:19:04,770 --> 00:19:08,790
There will be times when we disagree.

118
00:19:08,800 --> 00:19:10,130
But I promise you this.

119
00:19:10,710 --> 00:19:16,970
I will always tell you the truth and nothing but the truth.

120
00:19:17,600 --> 00:19:23,630
I will serve you and only you.

121
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:27,110
I will listen when you disagree.

122
00:19:28,130 --> 00:19:29,990
I will admit when I am wrong.

123
00:19:29,990 --> 00:19:33,790
And I will never forget who sent me here.

124
00:19:35,130 --> 00:19:42,360
The power of this office does not belong to me.

125
00:19:42,560 --> 00:19:43,860
It belongs to you.

126
00:19:45,950 --> 00:19:57,120
And as excited as I am by the history we've made tonight, I pray it does not compare to the future we build together.

127
00:19:58,375 --> 00:20:09,060
The nation will look at Texas and say, "We've won something far more important than an election."

128
00:20:10,100 --> 00:20:16,060
They will look at Texas and say that faith in government has been restored.

129
00:20:17,040 --> 00:20:30,350
They will look at Texas and see the power of a government that lifts every single person up and never punches down.

130
00:20:32,210 --> 00:20:40,230
We will build a government more honest, more just, and worthy of the people who call Texas home.

131
00:20:40,710 --> 00:20:45,250
And we will never forget the simple truth that brought us here tonight.

132
00:20:46,030 --> 00:20:49,570
Texas belongs to the people of Texas.

133
00:20:50,629 --> 00:21:05,989
I can't help but think of my grandmother, Grandma Hinojosa, who used to tell me, 'No te dejes.'

134
00:21:05,999 --> 00:21:08,710
Know your worth, and fight to defend it.

135
00:21:10,630 --> 00:21:14,770
A lot of Latinas in Texas grew up hearing those same words.

136
00:21:15,770 --> 00:21:20,310
From their own mothers, their own abuelas.

137
00:21:20,310 --> 00:21:23,870
This year we lived them and we changed this state.

138
00:21:24,830 --> 00:21:27,550
And this win belongs to you and to them.

139
00:21:29,311 --> 00:21:38,410
And I need to thank some people here now who made this all possible.

140
00:21:41,840 --> 00:21:45,676
Pablo, no one has sacrificed more than you.

141
00:21:45,686 --> 00:21:53,536
You have been so supportive.

142
00:21:53,546 --> 00:22:01,020
You have been so supportive and gracious and I am so proud of you.

143
00:22:02,420 --> 00:22:16,640
Even though neither you nor Matteo ever asked for this, my fight comes from my deep love for the both of you and my desire to make this world safer and better

144
00:22:16,640 --> 00:22:18,120
For the both of you.

145
00:22:19,746 --> 00:22:30,740
You have been so understanding and encouraging and I thank you both so much.

146
00:22:31,420 --> 00:22:41,570
To my husband John who I made promise to never run for office.

147
00:22:45,250 --> 00:22:54,130
You have been the rock who has held it all down and sacrificed and stood beside me in the hardest fights.

148
00:22:55,030 --> 00:22:58,710
This is not possible without you and I love you.

149
00:23:00,110 --> 00:23:26,330
To my sister, Xochitl, who spent a year telling everyone who would listen that we would win, who believed so relentlessly and with such certainty that it finally came true.

150
00:23:29,200 --> 00:23:31,388
I love you, sis.

151
00:23:31,388 --> 00:23:34,122
You're the best sister a sister could ask for.

152
00:23:36,250 --> 00:23:43,350
Mom and Dad, Cyndi and Robert, my brothers and sisters, and my entire family: thank you.

153
00:23:43,830 --> 00:23:46,410
Thank you for working day and night.

154
00:23:46,554 --> 00:23:53,060
Everything I believe and love about this state is because of you.

155
00:23:53,060 --> 00:23:54,800
And I love all of you.

156
00:23:56,880 --> 00:24:07,157
To our next United States Senator, James Talarico.

157
00:24:07,167 --> 00:24:15,510
For years, we believed there had to be a different and better way forward.

158
00:24:16,270 --> 00:24:18,250
It looks like we were right.

159
00:24:22,040 --> 00:24:25,440
Thank you and congratulations, my friend.

160
00:24:25,440 --> 00:24:34,013
To Amy Friedman, my campaign [inaudible].

161
00:24:50,879 --> 00:24:54,610
You are an angel sent down from heaven to run this campaign.

162
00:24:55,350 --> 00:24:58,690
You believed in me and you believed in Texas.

163
00:24:59,550 --> 00:25:02,010
I will never forget all that you gave.

164
00:25:02,850 --> 00:25:04,770
All that you sacrificed to get us here.

165
00:25:06,050 --> 00:25:16,510
You led the best campaign team in the nation, a team that I hope gets some well-earned sleep tonight.

166
00:25:18,430 --> 00:25:26,790
To the people who showed up early for me and often, who posted when I could still keep track of who was tagging me,

167
00:25:27,360 --> 00:25:40,480
Whether it was 10 times a day from Houston or DMs spreading my message to Texas newcomers, who showed up at events when it was still only familiar faces.

168
00:25:41,700 --> 00:25:46,660
Who gave your labor and your love and you took a leap of faith.

169
00:25:47,140 --> 00:25:48,140
Thank you.

170
00:25:48,800 --> 00:25:54,790
Thank you.

171
00:25:54,840 --> 00:25:59,840
And to my hometown, Brownsville.

172
00:26:09,540 --> 00:26:21,240
Tonight, one of your own becomes the first governor of Texas from the Rio Grande Valley.

173
00:26:21,240 --> 00:26:24,690
We did it.

174
00:26:24,690 --> 00:26:28,140
We did it.

175
00:26:28,140 --> 00:26:31,840
Good night, and God bless Texas.